  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "This may seem like a minor nitpick, but as someone who has existed in male-dominated spaces a lot, I *always* notice these things.\nIn the art options in the new main menu, of the ones that depict a human character, 8 of them are male-presenting, and only one is possibly female.\nI had a hard time finding a background that felt like it was made with people like me in mind (I chose the jellies).  Yes, this is a small thing, but little stuff like this matters when trying to create an environment that welcomes everyone.\nThe art overall is wonderful, and I appreciate it a lot, but please keep in mind the outward message when compiling collections such as these and try to proactively include artists and styles of different genders.  Don't let it be an afterthought.",
